{"acronym":"AMBITION 1","arm_groups":[{"intervention_names":["Drug: Zenagamtide"],"label":"Zenagamtide","type":"EXPERIMENTAL"},{"intervention_names":["Drug: Placebo"],"label":"Placebo","type":"PLACEBO_COMPARATOR"}],"brief_summary":"This study is being done to look at how well zenagamtide lowers blood sugar levels and body weight in people with type 2 diabetes when compared to placebo. Participants will either get zenagamtide, the treatment being tested or placebo, a treatment that has no active medicine in it. Which treatment participants get is decided by chance. Zenagamtide is a new medicine that doctors cannot prescribe yet, but it has been tested in humans before.","brief_title":"A Research Study Investigating How Well Zenagamtide Lowers Blood Sugar and Body Weight Compared to Placebo in People With Type 2 Diabetes Treated With Diet and Exercise","collaborators":[],"completion_date":{"date":"2028-08-28","type":"ESTIMATED"},"conditions":["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"],"design":{"allocation":"RANDOMIZED","intervention_model":"PARALLEL","masking":"QUADRUPLE","primary_purpose":"TREATMENT","who_masked":["PARTICIPANT","CARE_PROVIDER","INVESTIGATOR","OUTCOMES_ASSESSOR"]},"eligibility":{"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n\n* Male or female (sex assigned at birth, inclusive of all gender identities).\n* Age 18 years or above at the time of signing the informed consent.\n* Diagnosed with type 2 diabetes (T2D) greater than or equal to (≥) 30 days before screening.\n* Treatment naïve to any glucose-lowering medication(s).\n\nExclusion criteria:\n\n* Female who is pregnant, breast-feeding or intends to become pregnant or is of childbearing potential and not using adequate contraceptive method.\n* Current treatment or history of treatment with any medication for the indication of diabetes, or treatment with glucagon-like-peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonists (RA), dual GLP-1/gastric inhibitory peptide (GIP) RAs (or any other GLP-1 based treatment) or amylin analogues for any indication. However, previous insulin treatment during Gestational Diabetes Mellitus is allowed.\n* Treatment with any medication for the indication of obesity before screening.\n* Participant with diabetic retinopathy or maculopathy who received treatment with retinal photocoagulation, vitrectomy or anti-Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor (anti-VEGF) within 180 days before screening or are expected to require treatment within 180 days after screening. Diabetic retinopathy or maculopathy must be verified by an eye examination performed within 90 days before screening or in the period between screening and randomisation. Pharmacological pupil-dilation is a requirement unless using a digital fundus photography camera specified for non-dilated examination.\n* Myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack or hospitalisation for unstable angina pectoris within 60 days before screening.\n* Chronic heart failure classified as being in New York Heart Association (NYHA) Class IV at screening.\n* Planned coronary, carotid or peripheral artery revascularisation.","healthy_volunteers":false,"maximum_age":null,"minimum_age":"18 Years","sex":"ALL","std_ages":["ADULT","OLDER_ADULT"]},"enrollment":{"count":200,"type":"ESTIMATED"},"first_posted":"2026-11-12","has_results":false,"interventions":[{"name":"Zenagamtide","other_names":[],"type":"DRUG"},{"name":"Placebo","other_names":[],"type":"DRUG"}],"last_known_status":null,"last_update_posted":"2026-11-12","lead_sponsor":{"class":"INDUSTRY","name":"Novo Nordisk A/S"},"nct_id":"NCT07931495","official_title":"Efficacy and Safety of Zenagamtide s.c. Once Weekly Compared to Placebo in Participants With Type 2 Diabetes Inadequately Controlled on Diet and Exercise","overall_status":"NOT_YET_RECRUITING","phases":["PHASE3"],"primary_completion_date":{"date":"2028-06-05","type":"ESTIMATED"},"primary_outcomes":[{"measure":"Change in glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c)","time_frame":"From baseline (week 0) to week 44"}],"results_first_posted":nu